{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_9","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"rg -n '\"'^#{1,4} |''^'\"\\\\| Archetype|\"'^'\"\\\\| Guardian' PLAN.md\"","aggregated_output":"1:# Build plan\n3:## Mandate and working method\n15:## Research and technical starting point\n17:### What the source establishes\n23:### Verified engine baseline; recheck at implementation time\n42:### Verified multiplayer baseline\n48:## The player experience\n50:### Core promise\n68:### Campaign and pacing\n86:### Tutorial and narrative\n92:## Rules and systemic design\n94:### Movement, visibility, and sound\n104:### Bow, ammunition, and bank shots\n120:### Enemy roster and guardians\n124:| Archetype | Behavior and clue | Player lesson | Initial durability |\n139:### Health, expedition failure, and checkpoints\n149:## Presentation, animation, and audio\n151:### Visual direction\n159:### Animation deliverables\n165:### Code-only audio\n173:## Controller-first UX and supported inputs\n197:## Attract mode, developer tools, and content handoff\n215:## Multiplayer architecture and lifecycle\n217:### One authority model for every mode\n227:### Standalone network transport\n237:### AI Hub integration\n255:## Implementation structure and delivery\n285:## Build sequence and completion gates\n287:### 1. Establish the real substrate\n293:### 2. Complete the central playable loop\n299:### 3. Finish the full expedition\n305:### 4. Finish the product systems\n311:### 5. Verify, tune, package, and deliver\n317:## Verification plan\n319:### One command and trustworthy evidence\n327:### Coverage matrix\n344:### Browser and presentation checks\n352:### AI Hub harness matrix\n367:## Final obligations and honest reporting\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
