{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_33","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"curl -L --fail --silent --show-error https://history.blueskyrangers.com/mattelelectronics/games/images/addcloudy/ADDCloudyScreen.gif -o research/source-screen.gif\nmagick research/source-screen.gif research/source-screen.png\nrg -n 'Shell|shell\\\\.|screens|settings.register|menu.items|open\\\\(' vendor/engine/API-INDEX.md | head -55\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_33","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"curl -L --fail --silent --show-error https://history.blueskyrangers.com/mattelelectronics/games/images/addcloudy/ADDCloudyScreen.gif -o research/source-screen.gif\nmagick research/source-screen.gif research/source-screen.png\nrg -n 'Shell|shell\\\\.|screens|settings.register|menu.items|open\\\\(' vendor/engine/API-INDEX.md | head -55\"","aggregated_output":"88:- 1184 21d. Shell; E.Shell: shell\n116:- `E.versionLabel()`: 'v0.7.0 · a1b2c3d 2026-10-07': the label to show on screens and in reports\n267:- `game.screen.scale = 'auto'`: how a fixed resolution fills the screen: 'sharp' (whole-number scale, every pixel the same size, black bars unless o.expand grows the picture into them), 'fill' (the la [... omitted end of long line]\n277:- `input.anyPressed()`: any action pressed this step (title screens: \"press any button\")\n318:- `input.touchButtons(actions, o = {})` †: On-screen buttons for phones and tablets (shown on touch screens; the player's settings can show them always or hide them, put them on the left, and size the [... omitted end of long line]\n364:- `E.font.title(g, s, x, y, o = {})`: Big logo text for title screens: scaled glyphs with a vertical color gradient, an outline and an extruded 3D edge. title(g, 'CASTLE OF NIGHT', x, y, { scale: 3, c [... omitted end of long line]\n466:- `new E.Game({ menu })`: the pause, settings and controls screens ({ items, settings, controls, quit } adjusts them, false leaves them out)\n555:- `game.shell = null` †: the E.Shell over this game (an HTML interface: screens and HUD), or null\n570:- `E.showError(title, e)`: show an error in the red box at the top of the page (the engine does it for errors in update and draw); a click hides it. Before play has started it shows on the boot screen [... omitted end of long line]\n592:- `E.diagnose(game = E.current)`: the report a bug needs, at any time (and on the boot screen when a game can't start): { engine, game, time, page, browser, device, screen, canvas, gpu, sound, storage [... omitted end of long line]\n637:- `saves.show(mode = 'load', done)` †: open the standard save screen over the game (E.Shell's): 'save' (to a slot) or 'load'; done(save) after a load or a save. False without a menu (a headless game,  [... omitted end of long line]\n1155:- `new E.Menu(game, items, o = {}) → menu`: Menu with a cursor (title screens, pause menus, shops, battle commands). const menu = new E.Menu(game, ['START', 'OPTIONS', { label: 'CONTINUE', disabled: ! [... omitted end of long line]\n1168:- `menu.items`: the entries (strings, or { label, disabled })\n1184:## 21d. Shell\n1186:- `new E.Shell(game, o = {}) → shell`: new E.Shell(game, { theme, screens: { name: spec }, settings: { items, onChange(settings, key) }, store: 'shell-settings', meters: .125, standard: true }): an HT [... omitted end of long line]\n1187:- `new E.Shell({ theme })`: CSS variables (ink, paper, accent, muted, danger, line, font: a family, titleFont), and scale: the whole interface that many times (a number, or a function of the window) f [... omitted end of long line]\n1188:- `new E.Shell({ screens })`: specs ui.show(name) starts from (the pause screen follows game.paused; screens: { pause: false } leaves it out)\n1189:- `new E.Shell({ settings })`: settings.items: the game's own settings, { key, label, type: 'toggle' | 'slider' | 'select', min, max, step, options, value } (kept in game.settings, beside the standard [... omitted end of long line]\n1190:- `new E.Shell({ store, meters })`: store: where an older version saved them; meters: meters per world unit for distances\n1191:- `new E.Shell({ standard })`: false leaves out the standard menu (the pause screen's Settings, Controls, Full screen and Quit, and the settings' groups)\n1192:- `shell.back()` †: what cancel does: the screen's own back(), or close it (back to the screen under it; closing the pause screen resumes)\n1193:- `shell.dispose()` †: take its elements away and let go of the game (game.dispose() does it)\n1194:- `shell.hide()` †: close every screen (and resume, when the menu paused the game)\n1195:- `shell.hud(st = {})` †: the HUD, from this step's state (call it every step; a piece left out is hidden, and only what changed is redrawn)\n1196:- `shell.hud({ objective })` †: { step: '01 / 04', title, text, at: { x, y, z }, from: hero } (the distance in meters, and above or below)\n1197:- `shell.hud({ status, place, tip })` †: status: 'UNSEEN' or { text, color }; place: 'The Old Harbour'; tip: 'text' or { title, text }\n1198:- `shell.hud({ bars, counts })` †: bars: [{ label, value, max, kind: 'bar' | 'pips', color }] (health, stamina, a meter); counts: [[label, value]]\n1199:- `shell.hud({ prompt })` †: { key: 'E' (or act: 'interact': its key on the player's device), label, hint, progress: 0..1 }\n1200:- `shell.hud({ keys, buttons })` †: keys: [['WASD', 'Move'], ...] (hidden on touch screens); buttons: [[label, fn or action]] (top right: pause and map where there is no Escape key)\n1201:- `shell.hud({ minimap })` †: { map, at (with facing), markers: [{ x, y, kind: 'dot' | 'diamond' | 'ring' | 'cross', color }], onClick(x, y) (the world point clicked), fog (an E.Fog: unseen cells blac [... omitted end of long line]\n1202:- `shell.screen` †: the name of the open screen ('pause', 'settings', 'controls', ...), or null while the game plays\n1203:- `shell.settings` †: the player's settings: game.settings (the standard ones and the game's own, by key)\n1204:- `shell.show(name, spec = {})` †: open a screen: 'title' | 'pause' | 'settings' | 'help' | 'results' | 'map' or a name of your own, from spec over o.screens[name]. A spec: { kicker, title, text (stri [... omitted end of long line]\n1205:- `shell.show('title')` †: { name, subtitle, meta: [...], footer }\n1206:- `shell.show('help')` †: { keys: [[key, what]], sections: [[heading, text]] }\n1207:- `shell.show('results')` †: { emblem, stats: [[value, label]], medals: [[label, earned]] }\n1208:- `shell.show('map')` †: { map, at, markers (a list or a function), labels: [[text, x, y]], onPick(x, y) }\n1209:- `shell.toast(title, text = '', seconds = 4)` †: a message that slides in at the top for a few seconds\n1210:- `shell.tutorial(title, text = '', seconds = 15)` †: a tutorial card (bottom left, dismissable) for some seconds; tutorial(null) takes it away\n1211:- `shell.root = null` †: game: the game it is over; o: its options; root: its DOM element (null in a headless game)\n1449:- `E.gen.open(rows)`: every floor cell ('.') of rows, as [x, y]\n1628:- `world.shellMap()`: the explored map for E.Shell's minimap: game.shell.hud({ minimap: world.shellMap() }) (a cell a square, the save and boss rooms marked, the hero's cell)\n1639:- `world.rooms`: every room by id: { id, def, map, at, w, h } (its size in screens)\n1718:- `strategy.minimap(colors = {})` †: E.Shell's minimap spec: the map, the fog, the camera's view, the units seen as dots by side, a click moving the camera\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_34","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"rg -n 'class Shell|show\\\\(name, spec|spec\\\\.content|spec\\\\.actions|e-shell|m3-shell|data-shell' vendor/engine/my-3d2dge.js | head -40\nsed -n '1184,1212p' vendor/engine/API-INDEX.md\nsed -n '160,245p' vendor/engine/kits/adventure.js\nsed -n '190,260p' vendor/engine/kits/roguelike.js\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_34","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"rg -n 'class Shell|show\\\\(name, spec|spec\\\\.content|spec\\\\.actions|e-shell|m3-shell|data-shell' vendor/engine/my-3d2dge.js | head -40\nsed -n '1184,1212p' vendor/engine/API-INDEX.md\nsed -n '160,245p' vendor/engine/kits/adventure.js\nsed -n '190,260p' vendor/engine/kits/roguelike.js\"","aggregated_output":"9415:class Shell {\n9479:  show(name, spec = {}) {\n## 21d. Shell\n\n- `new E.Shell(game, o = {}) → shell`: new E.Shell(game, { theme, screens: { name: spec }, settings: { items, onChange(settings, key) }, store: 'shell-settings', meters: .125, standard: true }): an HTML interface over the game (see the section's header)\n- `new E.Shell({ theme })`: CSS variables (ink, paper, accent, muted, danger, line, font: a family, titleFont), and scale: the whole interface that many times (a number, or a function of the window) for a TV across a room; tv: true picks one by the window's width (14 px text at 875 px, up to 30 at 1,875)\n- `new E.Shell({ screens })`: specs ui.show(name) starts from (the pause screen follows game.paused; screens: { pause: false } leaves it out)\n- `new E.Shell({ settings })`: settings.items: the game's own settings, { key, label, type: 'toggle' | 'slider' | 'select', min, max, step, options, value } (kept in game.settings, beside the standard ones)\n- `new E.Shell({ store, meters })`: store: where an older version saved them; meters: meters per world unit for distances\n- `new E.Shell({ standard })`: false leaves out the standard menu (the pause screen's Settings, Controls, Full screen and Quit, and the settings' groups)\n- `shell.back()` †: what cancel does: the screen's own back(), or close it (back to the screen under it; closing the pause screen resumes)\n- `shell.dispose()` †: take its elements away and let go of the game (game.dispose() does it)\n- `shell.hide()` †: close every screen (and resume, when the menu paused the game)\n- `shell.hud(st = {})` †: the HUD, from this step's state (call it every step; a piece left out is hidden, and only what changed is redrawn)\n- `shell.hud({ objective })` †: { step: '01 / 04', title, text, at: { x, y, z }, from: hero } (the distance in meters, and above or below)\n- `shell.hud({ status, place, tip })` †: status: 'UNSEEN' or { text, color }; place: 'The Old Harbour'; tip: 'text' or { title, text }\n- `shell.hud({ bars, counts })` †: bars: [{ label, value, max, kind: 'bar' | 'pips', color }] (health, stamina, a meter); counts: [[label, value]]\n- `shell.hud({ prompt })` †: { key: 'E' (or act: 'interact': its key on the player's device), label, hint, progress: 0..1 }\n- `shell.hud({ keys, buttons })` †: keys: [['WASD', 'Move'], ...] (hidden on touch screens); buttons: [[label, fn or action]] (top right: pause and map where there is no Escape key)\n- `shell.hud({ minimap })` †: { map, at (with facing), markers: [{ x, y, kind: 'dot' | 'diamond' | 'ring' | 'cross', color }], onClick(x, y) (the world point clicked), fog (an E.Fog: unseen cells black, seen ones dim), camera: true (the ground the screen shows) }\n- `shell.screen` †: the name of the open screen ('pause', 'settings', 'controls', ...), or null while the game plays\n- `shell.settings` †: the player's settings: game.settings (the standard ones and the game's own, by key)\n- `shell.show(name, spec = {})` †: open a screen: 'title' | 'pause' | 'settings' | 'help' | 'results' | 'map' or a name of your own, from spec over o.screens[name]. A spec: { kicker, title, text (strings or functions), actions: [[label, fn] or { label, fn, act, primary, disabled }], back (fn for cancel), rows: ['glyphs', 'invertY', '#A heading'] (settings' rows, changed as on the settings screen) }. From another screen it stacks (back() returns); shown again, it updates (the new spec over the old). 'settings' takes its items\n- `shell.show('title')` †: { name, subtitle, meta: [...], footer }\n- `shell.show('help')` †: { keys: [[key, what]], sections: [[heading, text]] }\n- `shell.show('results')` †: { emblem, stats: [[value, label]], medals: [[label, earned]] }\n- `shell.show('map')` †: { map, at, markers (a list or a function), labels: [[text, x, y]], onPick(x, y) }\n- `shell.toast(title, text = '', seconds = 4)` †: a message that slides in at the top for a few seconds\n- `shell.tutorial(title, text = '', seconds = 15)` †: a tutorial card (bottom left, dismissable) for some seconds; tutorial(null) takes it away\n- `shell.root = null` †: game: the game it is over; o: its options; root: its DOM element (null in a headless game)\n\n * SLICE 1  ADVENTURE  (Secret of Mana, Zelda: ALttP). Three rooms: village, ruins, shrine. Talk, clear the ruins for\n * the key, open the great door, claim the crystal. THE LOOK: wall MATERIALS, ONE floorTex with PAINTED LIGHT, pitched\n * roofs, leaf-clump bushes, light shafts, dialog PORTRAITS.\n * KEYS: WASD or arrows move, J or X swings the sword, Enter or Space talks. TOUCH: the stick, ATTACK, CONFIRM.\n * ANY SCREEN: rooms are 4:3 in a world that goes on past them (forest above and below, the next rooms beside), so a\n * screen of any shape is filled. CAMERA (Settings, or C): ROOMS slides screen by screen as Zelda's does, the rooms beside\n * this one under a dim CURTAIN (they wait, as their monsters do); SCROLL follows the hero. The HUD sits in the corners.\n * ===================================================================================== */\nconst ADV = (() => {\n  const T = 16, ROOM = [14 * T, 12 * T], AREAS = ['Mana Village', 'Mossy Ruins', 'Shrine of Mana'];\n  const ROWS = [\n    // village          ruins             shrine\n    ['^^^^^^^^^^^^^^', 'RRRRRRRRRRRRRR', 'XXXXXXXXXXXXXX'],\n    ['^^#^^^^^^^^#^^', 'RHhJKFYDYFKhHR', 'XwjiXnWXnXijwX'],\n    ['#UUUU.ZZZZ.~~#', 'R.u..qv.vq.S.R', 'X.S*.B..B.*S.X'],\n    ['#GQOQbzNzZu~~#', 'H.KK....x....H', 'X.....rA.....X'],\n    ['#ccccV~ccLe~~#', 'K..s.q::::.s.H', 'X..I..++..I..X'],\n    ['#cM@cPccac=~~#', 'H.....::::k..K', 'X....m++m....X'],\n    ['#,,,,,,,,,,__,', ',,....::C:...H', 'X4.I..++..I.4X'],\n    ['#.b...b.g,d__,', ',,..o.::::.s.H', 'X.....++.....X'],\n    ['#...%%%f..s~~#', 'Hb.K..::::q.KH', 'X..I..++..I..X'],\n    ['#T..%%%.u..~~#', 'H.u..s....y.RH', 'X.p...++...p.X'],\n    ['#.3........~~#', 'H...bK...b.xRH', 'X.....E+.....X'],\n    ['##############', 'RRRRRRRRRRRRRR', 'XXXXXX++XXXXXX']\n  ].map(r => r.join(''));\n  // the world AROUND the rooms: PAD rows of forest canopy above and below (a meadow's edge first, the shrine's stone under\n  // the shrine), so a screen of any shape is filled. The rooms' rows start at OY\n  const PAD = 12, OY = PAD * T, wood = (cx, cy) => cx >= 28 ? 'X' : E.hash2(cx * 7, cy * 5) < .18 ? '2' : '1';\n  const AROUND = (cy0, meadow) => Array.from({ length: PAD }, (_, i) => Array.from({ length: 42 }, (_, cx) => meadow && i < 2 && cx < 28 ? '.' : wood(cx, cy0 + i)).join(''));\n  ROWS.unshift(...AROUND(0)); ROWS.push(...AROUND(PAD + 12, true));\n  const LEGEND = {\n    // walls: a wall type (TYPES), or { tile, spawn } = a wall with a prop on its face (THINGS)\n    '#': 1, 'U': 5, 'Z': 8, 'R': 9, 'H': 3, 'K': 4, 'F': 6, 'X': 2, 'A': 7, '1': 10, '2': { tile: 10, spawn: 'tree' },\n    '^': { tile: 1, spawn: 'tree' }, 'G': { tile: 5, spawn: 'ivy' }, 'Q': { tile: 5, spawn: 'pane' }, 'O': { tile: 5, spawn: 'door' },\n    'z': { tile: 8, spawn: 'pane' }, 'N': { tile: 8, spawn: 'shop' }, 'h': { tile: 3, spawn: 'vines' }, 'J': { tile: 3, spawn: 'cobweb' }, 'Y': { tile: 6, spawn: 'moss' }, 'D': { tile: 6, spawn: 'gate' },\n    'w': { tile: 2, spawn: 'window' }, 'W': { tile: 2, spawn: 'rose' }, 'i': { tile: 2, spawn: 'torch' }, 'n': { tile: 2, spawn: 'banner' }, 'j': { tile: 2, spawn: 'cobweb' }, 'r': { tile: 7, spawn: 'relic' },\n    // floors: a tag for floorTex; block = not walkable\n    ',': { floor: 'path' }, 'c': { floor: 'plaza' }, '~': { floor: 'water', block: true }, '_': { floor: 'bridge' }, ':': { floor: 'pave' }, '+': { floor: 'carpet' }, '%': { floor: 'bed' },\n    '@': { floor: 'plaza', spawn: 'hero' }, 'M': { floor: 'plaza', spawn: 'elder' }, 'P': { floor: 'plaza', spawn: 'pot' }, 'L': { floor: 'plaza', spawn: 'lamp' },\n    'V': { floor: 'water', block: true, spawn: 'fountain' }, 'C': { floor: 'pave', spawn: 'chest' }, 'E': { floor: 'carpet', spawn: 'entry' }, 'd': { floor: 'path', spawn: 'villager' },\n    // people, creatures and props\n    'f': 'florist', 'a': { floor: 'plaza', spawn: 'cat' }, 's': 'rabite', 'v': 'bat', 'k': 'goblin', 'm': 'mage', 'b': 'bush', 'p': 'pot', 'T': 'oak', 'g': 'sign', 'u': 'mushroom',\n    'e': 'barrel', '=': 'crate', '3': 'stump', '4': 'obelisk', 'q': 'ruin', 'I': 'pillar', 'S': 'statue', 'o': 'rock', 'x': 'crystal', 'y': 'skull', 'B': 'brazier', '*': 'candelabra'\n  };\n  // wall MATERIALS: face = side, roof = top pattern (beam = timber); cut = lowered to cutH in front of the camera\n  const SLAB = { face: 'stone', roof: 'slab' }, TYPES = {\n    1: { h: 16, cut: true, cutH: 7, face: 'hedge', roof: 'leaves', top: '#3f8c3c', side: '#2e6a34' },   // hedge\n    2: { h: 34, cut: true, cutH: 8, ...SLAB, top: '#4e4670', side: '#6a6294', course: 9 },   // shrine stone\n    3: { h: 26, cut: true, cutH: 8, face: 'ruin', roof: 'slab', top: '#7a8a66', side: '#8e8a98' },   // ruin wall, mossy top: the 'ruin' MATERIAL (stones, cracks, moss, dirt; docs/ASSETS.md)\n    4: { h: 12, cut: true, ...SLAB, top: '#72845e', side: '#8e8a98', course: 6 },   // crumbled ruin\n    5: { h: 36, face: 'timber', roof: 'tiles', top: '#c4583a', side: '#f0e0c0', beam: '#6a4228' },   // cottage\n    6: { h: 36, ...SLAB, top: '#5a5480', side: '#7a7298', course: 9 },   // shrine facade\n    7: { h: 9, ...SLAB, top: '#8a84b4', side: '#5a5484', course: 4 },   // altar\n    8: { h: 36, face: 'plaster', roof: 'tiles', top: '#3a7ab4', side: '#f4e6c8' },   // shop\n    9: { h: 30, cut: true, cutH: 8, face: 'rock', roof: 'grass', top: '#5a9a44', side: '#8a7462' },   // cliff\n    10: { h: 22, face: 'hedge', roof: 'leaves', top: '#2c6a36', side: '#1f4a2a' }   // the forest round the rooms\n  };\n  // set dressing: tag -> prop(s). r = solid, cut = breakable (debris), drop = loot, face = on the wall at z (anchor\n  // 'top' hangs it), light = GPU light, dx = nudge, hidden = appears later; shape = a SHAPE (E.SHAPES, docs/ASSETS.md:\n  // right in every view and turn, no drawing code) in place of a prop, size its scale\n  const THINGS = {\n    // village\n    door: [{ face: true, size: 1.1, color: '#7a4222' }, { prop: 'lantern', face: true, z: 33, dx: 14, anchor: 'top', light: '#ffb060' }],\n    shop: [{ prop: 'door', face: true, size: 1.1, color: '#2a4a7a' }, { prop: 'awning', face: true, z: 23, size: .95, color: '#d8483a' }],\n    pane: { prop: 'window', face: true, z: 12, size: .65, color: '#6a4424', colors: ['#fff0b0', '#ffd070'] }, ivy: { prop: 'vines', face: true, z: 35, anchor: 'top', color: '#3a8a3a', blossom: '#f890b0' },\n    fountain: { prop: 'statue', size: .8, color: '#a8a6c0', dx: 8 }, lamp: { prop: 'streetlamp', r: 3, size: .8, halo: false }, oak: { prop: 'tree', size: 1.45, r: 8 },   // lamp: unlit by day\n    bush: { r: 6, cut: ['#2f7a34', '#5ab04a', '#9ad86a'] }, pot: { size: .95, r: 5, cut: ['#7a3a22', '#c07040', '#e8a878'], drop: 'gem' }, sign: { r: 4 },\n    mushroom: { size: .75, color: '#e0503a' }, barrel: { shape: 'barrel', r: 5, size: .75 }, crate: { shape: 'crate', r: 6, size: .65 },\n    // from the asset store, cut into the page's 'adventure' set (src/assets/sets/adventure.js); without it, props\n    ...(E.addAssets((window.ASSETS || {}).adventure || { set: 'adventure' }).shapes.length ? { stump: { shape: 'adventure:stump-round', r: 5, size: .7 },\n      obelisk: { shape: 'adventure:pillar-obelisk', r: 6, size: .8 } } : { stump: { prop: 'rock', r: 5, color: '#8a5a3a' }, obelisk: { prop: 'pillar', r: 6 } }),\n    // ruins\n    vines: { face: true, z: 25, anchor: 'top', color: '#4a8a3a', blossom: '#f890b0' }, moss: { prop: 'vines', face: true, z: 35, anchor: 'top', size: .8, color: '#5a8a3a', blossom: '#f890b0' },\n    gate: { prop: 'door', face: true, size: 1.1, color: '#5a3a6a' }, ruin: { prop: 'pillar', broken: true, r: 7 }, rock: { r: 5, color: '#8a8698' }, skull: { prop: 'bones' },\n    crystal: { r: 4, light: '#5ad8f0' }, chest: { r: 6, hidden: true },\n    // shrine\n    window: { face: true, z: 7, size: .8, colors: ['#e05a6a', '#5a8ae8', '#f0c85a', '#6ad08a'], light: '#8ab0ff' }, torch: { face: true, z: 14, light: '#ff9a4a' },\n    rose: { prop: 'window', face: true, z: 2, size: 1, dx: 8, colors: ['#e8c85a', '#c04aa0', '#5a8ae8'], light: '#c8a0ff' }, banner: { face: true, z: 8, size: .8, color: '#8a1a3a', emblem: '#e8c04a' },\n    cobweb: { face: true, z: 34, anchor: 'top', size: .9 }, pillar: { r: 7 }, statue: { r: 6, color: '#9a98b0' }, brazier: { r: 5, size: .9, light: '#ff9a4a' }, candelabra: { r: 3, size: .8, light: '#ffc060' }\n  };\n  // palettes: E.ramp(hex, n, strength) = n hue-shifted shades, dark to light\n  const rgb = hexes => hexes.map(E.hex), R5 = (c, s = .6) => rgb(E.ramp(c, 5, s)), FLAG = (s, mortar) => ({ stones: s.slice(1, 4), mortar, hi: s[4], lo: s[0], speck: s[1] });\n  const GRASS = [['#4c9a3e', '#5aa640', '#6cb44c'], ['#42804a', '#4a8a48', '#5a9a4e']].map(room => room.map(c => R5(c))), DIRT = R5('#b08652', .7), WATER = R5('#2a7ac4', .9), STONE = R5('#a49a8a', .7), SOIL = R5('#6e4a34');\n  const PLAZA = FLAG(R5('#b4a894'), E.hex('#6a5e52')), PAVE = FLAG(R5('#8a8a96'), E.hex('#3a3a3e')), TILE = [R5('#5a5688'), R5('#403c68')], PETAL = rgb(['#ffffff', '#ffe070', '#f890b0']);\n  const CARPET = rgb(E.ramp('#9a2438', 4)), GOLD = rgb(E.ramp('#d8a840', 3)), RUNE = [...E.hex('#6ae8e0'), .35], LILY = R5('#4aa050');   // 4th value = GPU glow\n  const SKY = rgb(['#a8dcf4', '#e8f8ff']), REFLECT = E.hex('#1e5a5a');   // sky glints, the hedge's reflection\n  const BLADES = [['DAGGER', 1], ['SWORD', 3], ['BROADSWORD', 5], ['RUNEBLADE', 8]];   // a better blade on most floors\n  const SPR = {   // the floor's things, in pixels\n    potion: E.sprite(['.cc.', '.ww.', 'wrrw', 'rRrr', 'rrrr', '.rr.'], { c: '#c8a070', w: '#e8e8f0', r: '#d02a3a', R: '#ff8a8a' }),\n    scroll: E.sprite(['bbbbbb', 'pwwwwp', 'pwkwkp', 'pwwwwp', 'bbbbbb'], { b: '#8a5a2a', p: '#c8b088', w: '#f0e4c0', k: '#5a4a3a' }),\n    blade: E.sprite(['....w', '...wl', '..wl.', 'gwl..', '.g...', 'h.g..'], { w: '#f0f0f8', l: '#a8b0c0', g: '#c8a040', h: '#6a4a2a' }),\n    gold: E.sprite(['.yy.', 'yYYy', 'yYyy', '.yy.'], { y: '#e0a020', Y: '#fff0a0' }),\n    amulet: E.sprite(['.g.g.', 'g...g', '.grg.', '.rRr.', '..r..'], { g: '#e0c050', r: '#e03a2a', R: '#ffb080' })\n  };\n  const PAVE = { stones: ['#3e3a44', '#46424c', '#423e48'].map(E.hex), mortar: E.hex('#1e1a24'), hi: E.hex('#524e58'), lo: E.hex('#2e2a34'), speck: E.hex('#4a4650') };\n  let R = Math.random, seed = 1, depth = 1, level = null, map = null, grid = null, fog = null, turns = null;\n  let hero = null, foes = [], items = [], braziers = [], log = [], travel = null, busy = 0, mode = 'play', over = null, dirWait = 0, lastDir = null, repeatT = 0, held = 0, going = false;\n  let stats = { kills: 0, gold: 0, turns: 0, killer: null };\n  const menu = new E.Menu(game, ['RETRY', 'TITLE'], { y: 0, onPick: i => i === 0 ? game.go('roguelike', null, { fade: 'iris' }) : game.go('title') });\n  const say = (s, c = '#e8e0d0') => { log.push({ s, c, t: game.real }); if (log.length > 4) log.shift(); };\n  const at = (x, y) => [x, y].join();\n  const occupied = (cx, cy) => (hero && hero.cx === cx && hero.cy === cy) || foes.some(f => !f.dead && f.cx === cx && f.cy === cy);\n  const foeAt = (cx, cy) => foes.find(f => !f.dead && f.cx === cx && f.cy === cy);\n  const center = (cx, cy) => [(cx + .5) * T, (cy + .5) * T];\n\n  /* ---- 1. A FLOOR: E.gen's rows by depth, its marks read by a TileMap; the grid, the fog and the turns over it ---- */\n  function build() {\n    const g = depth <= 3 ? E.gen.rooms(FW, FH, { seed: seed * 31 + depth, rooms: 10 }) : depth <= 6 ? E.gen.bsp(FW, FH, { seed: seed * 31 + depth, min: 8 }) : E.gen.cave(FW, FH, { seed: seed * 31 + depth, fill: .44 });\n    const sub = (ch, n, far) => E.gen.mark(g, ch, n, { seed: seed * 97 + depth * 13 + ch.charCodeAt(0), far, near: 2 });\n    const rows = g.rows.map(r => r.split('')); rows[g.end[1]][g.end[0]] = depth === LAST ? 'A' : '>'; g.rows = rows.map(r => r.join(''));\n    const pool = Object.keys(KINDS).filter(k => KINDS[k].from <= depth);\n    for (let i = 0; i < 5 + depth; i++) sub(KINDS[pool[Math.floor(R() * pool.length)]].name[0].toLowerCase(), 1, 6);\n    sub('!', 2 + (depth % 2), 3); sub('?', depth % 3 === 1 ? 1 : 0, 3); sub('$', 3, 2);\n    if (depth % 3 !== 0 && depth < LAST) sub(')', 1, 4);\n    const legend = { '#': 1, '>': 'stairs', A: 'amulet', '!': 'potion', '?': 'scroll', '$': 'gold', ')': 'blade' };\n    for (const k in KINDS) legend[KINDS[k].name[0].toLowerCase()] = k;\n    map = new E.TileMap({ rows: g.rows, legend, types: { 1: { h: 20, top: '#2e2a38', side: '#58506a', face: 'stone', roof: 'plain', cut: true, cutH: 4 } },\n      floorTex: (x, y) => E.tex.flagstone(x, y, PAVE, 16) });\n    map.outside = '#05040a';\n    level = g; grid = E.Grid.from(map, { diagonal: true }); fog = new E.Fog(grid); going = false;\n    foes = []; items = []; braziers = (g.rooms || []).filter((_, i) => i % 2 === 0).map(r => center(r.x, r.y));\n    for (const s of map.spawns) {\n      if (KINDS[s.tag]) foes.push(makeFoe(s.tag, s.cx, s.cy));\n      else if (['potion', 'scroll', 'gold', 'blade', 'amulet', 'stairs'].includes(s.tag)) items.push({ kind: s.tag, cx: s.cx, cy: s.cy });\n    }\n    const [sx, sy] = g.start; hero.cx = sx; hero.cy = sy; [hero.x, hero.y] = center(sx, sy); travel = null;\n    turns = new E.Turns([hero, ...foes], { mode: 'speed' });\n    game.follow(hero, { z: 12 }); game.cam.bounds = v => map.bounds(v); game.cam.snap = true;\n    say(depth === LAST ? 'THE AMULET IS NEAR' : 'FLOOR ' + depth, '#ffd890');\n    nextTurn();\n  }\n  function makeFoe(kind, cx, cy) {\n    const K = KINDS[kind], [x, y] = center(cx, cy), hp = K.hp + Math.floor((depth - K.from) * .8);\n    return { kind, K, cx, cy, x, y, hp, max: hp, atk: K.atk + Math.floor((depth - K.from) / 3), def: K.def, speed: K.speed, face: Math.PI / 2, awake: false, hit: 0, dead: false, die: 0,\n      rig: K.blob ? new E.Blob(K.blob) : new E.Humanoid(K.rig), swing: new E.Attack('slash') };\n  }\n\n  /* ---- 2. TURNS: the hero acts on input; then everyone faster than the next hero turn, by E.Turns ---- */\n  function nextTurn() {\n    for (let guard = 0; guard < 400; guard++) {\n      const a = turns.next(); if (!a) return;\n      if (a === hero) break;\n      if (!a.dead) foeTurn(a);\n      if (hero.hp <= 0) return;\n    }\n    fog.update([{ cx: hero.cx, cy: hero.cy, r: SIGHT }]);\n    for (const f of foes) if (!f.dead && !f.awake && fog.visible([f.cx, f.cy])) { f.awake = true; travel = null; say('A ' + f.K.name + ' SEES YOU', '#ffb070'); }\n  }\n  // a step: the cell changes now, the rig walks there in a tween\n  function stepTo(a, cx, cy) {\n    a.face = Math.atan2(cy - a.cy, cx - a.cx); a.cx = cx; a.cy = cy;\n    const [x, y] = center(cx, cy); if (a.tw) a.tw.cancel(); a.tw = game.tween(a, { x, y }, STEP, { ease: 'linear' });\n    if (a.rig && a.rig.kick) a.rig.kick(2);\n  }\n  function strike(a, d) {\n    a.face = Math.atan2(d.cy - a.cy, d.cx - a.cx); a.swing.start();\n    const dmg = Math.max(1, a.atk + Math.floor(R() * 3) - d.def);\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_35","type":"agent_message","text":"The source research confirms the key mechanics: scarce arrows, ricochet risk, sound and tracks as warnings, and the axe → boat → key route. I’m keeping those at the center of the expedition, with separate work underway on the authored chambers, creature rigs, and networking.\n"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_36","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"sed -n '9415,9540p' vendor/engine/my-3d2dge.js\nrg -n 'Adventure|Fog|camera|frame order|Custom.*draw|ground view' vendor/engine/AI_GUIDE.md | head -25\nrg -n '\"'^'\"\\\\.e|\\\\.shell|m3-shell|\\\\.e2|shell-panel' vendor/engine/my-3d2dge.js | head -30\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_36","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"sed -n '9415,9540p' vendor/engine/my-3d2dge.js\nrg -n 'Adventure|Fog|camera|frame order|Custom.*draw|ground view' vendor/engine/AI_GUIDE.md | head -25\nrg -n '\"'^'\"\\\\.e|\\\\.shell|m3-shell|\\\\.e2|shell-panel' vendor/engine/my-3d2dge.js | head -30\"","aggregated_output":"class Shell {\n  /**\n   * new E.Shell(game, { theme, screens: { name: spec }, settings: { items, onChange(settings, key) }, store: 'shell-settings',\n   * meters: .125, standard: true }): an HTML interface over the game (see the section's header)\n   * - theme: CSS variables (ink, paper, accent, muted, danger, line, font: a family, titleFont), and scale: the whole\n   *   interface that many times (a number, or a function of the window) for a TV across a room; tv: true picks one by\n   *   the window's width (14 px text at 875 px, up to 30 at 1,875)\n   * - screens: specs ui.show(name) starts from (the pause screen follows game.paused; screens: { pause: false } leaves it out)\n   * - settings: settings.items: the game's own settings, { key, label, type: 'toggle' | 'slider' | 'select', min, max,\n   *   step, options, value } (kept in game.settings, beside the standard ones)\n   * - store, meters: store: where an older version saved them; meters: meters per world unit for distances\n   * - standard: false leaves out the standard menu (the pause screen's Settings, Controls, Full screen and Quit, and the\n   *   settings' groups)\n   */\n  constructor(game, o = {}) {\n    if (game.shell && game.shell._sys && !o.system) game.shell.dispose();   // the game's own shell takes over from the engine's\n    /** game: the game it is over; o: its options; root: its DOM element (null in a headless game) */\n    this._game = game; this._o = o; this.root = null; this._stack = []; this._keep = new Set(); this._held = new Set(); this._last = {};\n    this._sys = !!o.system; this._std = o.standard !== false && game.o.menu !== false;\n    const old = store.get(o.store || 'shell-settings', null) || {}, S = game.settings;   // (settings saved by an older version are kept)\n    for (const it of this._items()) if (!S.spec(it.key)) { if (S._raw[it.key] === undefined && old[it.key] !== undefined) S._raw[it.key] = old[it.key]; S.define(Object.assign({ group: 'Game' }, it)); }\n    for (const k of ['sound', 'volume', 'motion']) if (S._raw[k] === undefined && old[k] !== undefined && this._items().some(it => it.key === k)) S.set(k, old[k]);\n    if (o.settings && o.settings.onChange) S.onChange = k => o.settings.onChange(S, k);\n    game.shell = this;\n    if (!this._sys && this._pauseSpec()) game.pauseOverlay = false;\n    if (game.headless || typeof document === 'undefined') return;\n    // rebinding: the next key or mouse button goes to the action being bound (before the game's own listeners see it)\n    const signal = game._abort ? game._abort.signal : undefined;\n    addEventListener('keydown', e => { const c = this._cap; if (!c) return; e.preventDefault(); e.stopImmediatePropagation(); if (e.code === 'Escape') this._capEnd('Not changed.'); else if (c.device === 'keys' && !e.repeat) this._capBind(e.code); }, { capture: true, signal });\n    addEventListener('pointerdown', e => { const c = this._cap; if (!c || c.device !== 'keys' || e.pointerType !== 'mouse') return; e.preventDefault(); e.stopImmediatePropagation(); this._capBind('Mouse' + e.button); }, { capture: true, signal });\n    addEventListener('wheel', e => { const c = this._cap; if (!c || c.device !== 'keys' || !e.deltaY) return; e.preventDefault(); e.stopImmediatePropagation(); this._capBind(e.deltaY < 0 ? 'WheelUp' : 'WheelDown'); }, { capture: true, signal, passive: false });\n    if (!document.getElementById('esh-css')) { const st = document.createElement('style'); st.id = 'esh-css'; st.textContent = SHELL_CSS; document.head.appendChild(st); }\n    const r = this.root = this._el('div', 'esh' + (game._corner ? ' esh-cornered' : '')), th = Object.assign({}, SHELL_THEME, o.theme);   // (the top-right column starts below the corner's buttons)\n    for (const k in th) r.style.setProperty('--' + (k === 'titleFont' ? 'title' : k), th[k]);\n    if (th.font && /\\d|\\b(bold|italic|normal|oblique)\\b/.test(th.font)) warn('shell:font', 'E.Shell theme.font is a family (\"Georgia, serif\"), not a CSS shorthand (\"' + th.font + '\"): the size comes from theme.scale');\n    const K = th.scale !== undefined ? th.scale : o.tv ? () => clamp(innerWidth * .016, 18, 30) / 14 : 1;   // (for ten feet: the whole interface that many times, still filling the window)\n    if (K !== 1) { const fit = () => { const k = Math.max(.25, +(typeof K === 'function' ? K(window) : K) || 1); Object.assign(r.style, { transform: 'scale(' + k + ')', transformOrigin: '0 0', inset: 'auto', left: '0', top: '0', width: 100 / k + 'vw', height: 100 / k + 'vh' }); }; fit(); addEventListener('resize', fit, { signal }); }\n    const host = document.body; host.appendChild(r);\n    const E2 = (cls, parent = r, tag = 'div') => { const e = this._el(tag, cls); e.hidden = true; parent.appendChild(e); return e; };\n    const col = this._el('div', 'esh-col'); r.appendChild(col);\n    /** the HUD's elements, by piece (hb, obj, vit, toast, tut, pr, tip, place, mini, keys) and the screen layer (scr) */\n    this._els = { hb: E2('esh-hb', col), obj: E2('esh-obj esh-pan'), vit: E2('esh-vit esh-pan', col), place: E2('esh-place', col), tip: E2('esh-tip esh-pan'), pr: E2('esh-pr esh-pan'), keys: E2('esh-keys'),\n      tut: E2('esh-tut esh-pan'), mini: E2('esh-mini', r, 'canvas'), toast: E2('esh-toast esh-pan'), scr: this._el('div', '') };\n    r.appendChild(this._els.scr); this._els.toast.hidden = false;\n    const mini = this._els.mini; mini.width = 176; mini.height = 158;\n    mini.onclick = e => { const m = this._miniLast, X = mini._xf; if (!m || !m.onClick) return; const rc = mini.getBoundingClientRect(), u = (e.clientX - rc.left) * mini.width / (rc.width || 1), v = (e.clientY - rc.top) * mini.height / (rc.height || 1); m.onClick(X ? (u - X.ox) / X.k : 0, X ? (v - X.oy) / X.k : 0); };   // (the world point clicked: a strategy game's camera goes there)\n  }\n  /** the name of the open screen ('pause', 'settings', 'controls', ...), or null while the game plays */\n  get screen() { const t = this._stack[this._stack.length - 1]; return t ? t.name : null; }\n  /** the player's settings: game.settings (the standard ones and the game's own, by key) */\n  get settings() { return this._game.settings; }\n  /** the pause screen's spec ({} for the standard one), or null without one */\n  _pauseSpec() { const sc = this._o.screens; return sc && 'pause' in sc ? sc.pause || null : this._std ? {} : null; }\n  /** does this shell give the standard menu (the corner's menu button and game.menu() open it)? */\n  _menu() { return this._std; }\n  /** open a screen: 'title' | 'pause' | 'settings' | 'help' | 'results' | 'map' or a name of your own, from spec over\n   *  o.screens[name]. A spec: { kicker, title, text (strings or functions), actions: [[label, fn] or { label, fn, act,\n   *  primary, disabled }], back (fn for cancel), rows: ['glyphs', 'invertY', '#A heading'] (settings' rows, changed as on\n   *  the settings screen) }. From another screen it stacks (back() returns); shown again, it updates\n   *  (the new spec over the old). 'settings' takes its items\n   *  - 'title': { name, subtitle, meta: [...], footer }\n   *  - 'help': { keys: [[key, what]], sections: [[heading, text]] }\n   *  - 'results': { emblem, stats: [[value, label]], medals: [[label, earned]] }\n   *  - 'map': { map, at, markers (a list or a function), labels: [[text, x, y]], onPick(x, y) } */\n  show(name, spec = {}) {\n    const top = this._stack[this._stack.length - 1], again = top && top.name === name, s = Object.assign({}, this._o.screens && this._o.screens[name], again ? top.s : null, spec);\n    if (again) this._stack.pop();   // the same screen again: updated in place\n    else { if (top) top.focus = this._focusAt(); this._status = ''; }   // (the focus comes back here when the new screen closes)\n    this._stack.push({ name, s, focus: again ? top.focus : undefined }); this._capEnd(); this._render(); return this;\n  }\n  /** what cancel does: the screen's own back(), or close it (back to the screen under it; closing the pause screen resumes) */\n  back() {\n    const top = this._stack[this._stack.length - 1]; if (!top) return this;\n    if (top.s.back) { top.s.back(); return this; }\n    this._stack.pop(); this._capEnd(); if (top.name === 'pause') this._game.resume();\n    this._closed(); this._render(); return this;\n  }\n  /** close every screen (and resume, when the menu paused the game) */\n  hide() { const p = this._stack.some(t => t.name === 'pause'); this._stack.length = 0; this._capEnd(); if (p) this._game.resume(); this._closed(); this._render(); return this; }\n  /** the last screen closed: a game the menu paused (a title under its settings) goes on */\n  _closed() { if (!this._stack.length && this._ownPause) { this._ownPause = false; this._game.resume(); } }\n  /** which focusable element of the open screen has the focus (its index), or -1 */\n  _focusAt() { if (!this.root) return -1; const all = this._focusables(); return all.indexOf(document.activeElement); }\n  _focusables() { return [...this._els.scr.querySelectorAll('.esh-sh button:not(:disabled), .esh-sh input:not(:disabled)')]; }\n  /** close the menu: every screen over the title (a game's own title screen stays), resuming a game the menu paused */\n  _close() { const i = this._stack.findIndex(t => t.name === 'title'); if (i < 0) return this.hide(); this._stack.length = i + 1; this._capEnd(); this._render(); return this; }\n  /** a close or back button over the screen (an icon, 44 px; the keys have Escape and Start, so it takes no focus) */\n  _navBtn(cls, label, d, fn) {\n    const b = this._el('button', 'esh-nav ' + cls); b.type = 'button'; b.tabIndex = -1; b.setAttribute('aria-label', label); b.title = label; b.innerHTML = cornerIcon(d);\n    b.onclick = e => { e.stopPropagation(); fn(); }; return b;\n  }\n  /** a sideways swipe on a screen goes back: the panel follows the finger and goes back past 70 px (a slider keeps its own) */\n  _swipe(sh, box, title) {\n    if (title) return; let s0 = null, swiped = false;\n    const end = e => { if (!s0 || e.pointerId !== s0.id) return; const dx = e.clientX - s0.x, go = s0.on && Math.abs(dx) > 70 && e.type === 'pointerup'; swiped = s0.on; s0 = null;\n      box.classList.add('esh-sw'); box.style.transform = go ? 'translateX(' + Math.sign(dx) * 110 + '%)' : ''; box.style.opacity = go ? '0' : '';\n      if (go) setTimeout(() => this.back(), 120); };\n    sh.addEventListener('pointerdown', e => { swiped = false; if (e.pointerType === 'mouse' || s0 || (e.target.closest && e.target.closest('input'))) return; s0 = { id: e.pointerId, x: e.clientX, y: e.clientY, on: false }; box.classList.remove('esh-sw'); });\n    sh.addEventListener('click', e => { if (swiped) { e.stopPropagation(); e.preventDefault(); swiped = false; } }, true);   // (the button a swipe began on isn't pressed)\n    sh.addEventListener('pointermove', e => {\n      if (!s0 || e.pointerId !== s0.id) return; const dx = e.clientX - s0.x, dy = e.clientY - s0.y;\n      if (!s0.on && Math.abs(dx) > 14 && Math.abs(dx) > Math.abs(dy) * 1.3) s0.on = true;\n      if (s0.on) { box.style.transform = 'translateX(' + dx + 'px)'; box.style.opacity = String(clamp(1 - Math.abs(dx) / 300, .3, 1)); }\n    });\n    for (const t of ['pointerup', 'pointercancel']) sh.addEventListener(t, end);\n  }\n  /** a message that slides in at the top for a few seconds */\n  toast(title, text = '', seconds = 4) {\n    if (!this.root) return this;\n    const e = this._els.toast; e.replaceChildren(this._el('b', '', title)); if (text) e.appendChild(this._el('p', 'esh-m', text));\n    e.classList.add('on'); this._toastEnd = this._game.real + seconds; return this;\n  }\n  /** a tutorial card (bottom left, dismissable) for some seconds; tutorial(null) takes it away */\n  tutorial(title, text = '', seconds = 15) {\n    if (!this.root) return this;\n    const e = this._els.tut; e.hidden = !title; this._tutEnd = title ? this._game.real + seconds : 0; if (!title) return this;\n    const x = this._el('button', 'esh-x', '×'); x.setAttribute('aria-label', 'Dismiss'); x.onclick = () => this.tutorial(null);\n    e.replaceChildren(this._el('div', 'esh-k', 'Tutorial'), this._el('b', '', title), this._el('p', 'esh-m', text), x); return this;\n  }\n  /**\n   * the HUD, from this step's state (call it every step; a piece left out is hidden, and only what changed is redrawn)\n   * - objective: { step: '01 / 04', title, text, at: { x, y, z }, from: hero } (the distance in meters, and above or below)\n   * - status, place, tip: status: 'UNSEEN' or { text, color }; place: 'The Old Harbour'; tip: 'text' or { title, text }\n   * - bars, counts: bars: [{ label, value, max, kind: 'bar' | 'pips', color }] (health, stamina, a meter); counts: [[label,\n   *   value]]\n   * - prompt: { key: 'E' (or act: 'interact': its key on the player's device), label, hint, progress: 0..1 }\n5:A coding agent that reads files gets the handoff package (`dist/handoff/`: the full engine readable, the cards, the tools, every 2D kit's game and a template game) or the agent edition alone (`dist/my [... omitted end of long line]\n19:1. **The world is 3D, the camera is 2D.** Game logic works in world units: x east, y south, z up, one tile = 16 units. A `View` projects world points to screen pixels. Switch the view and the same gam [... omitted end of long line]\n61:- *Klonoa and 2.5D platformers:* PlatformMap in the `brawler` view (tiles show their top faces), a bright `'day'` or `'forest'` backdrop, props in front of and behind the play plane (`y` of -12 and +1 [... omitted end of long line]\n124:1. The clock adds the frame's real time (at most 50 ms) to what is left from the last frame, and runs one step for each whole 1/120 s of it: 2 steps a frame at 60 Hz, 1 at 120 Hz, 1 or 0 at 144 Hz. Ea [... omitted end of long line]\n127:2. The renderer clears the buffer and positions the camera.\n135:   6. the frame is presented with a sub-pixel camera offset.\n147:- `res` with `expand: true` (what the starter kits use) fills any window with no bars: `res` is the least the screen shows, and `r.W` × `r.H` grows on the long side (a 16:9 monitor shows about 427×240 [... omitted end of long line]\n151:A scene is `{ enter(data), exit(), update(dt), draw(r), pausable, view, views, input, res, expand, touch, camera }`.\n152:- `game.go('play', data)` switches before the next step; timers, tweens, scripts and particles are cleared (weather too) and the camera snaps. `{ fade: 'iris', at: hero }` (or `'wipe'`, `'mosaic'`, `' [... omitted end of long line]\n158:- `cam.room = [w, h]` snaps the target to the center of the current room; the camera then slides, so Zelda- and Metroid-style room transitions come for free. Freeze gameplay while `cam.moving` is true [... omitted end of long line]\n159:- The player's zoom: a scene's `camera: { zoom: [.75, 2], start: 1, tall: 1.5 }` sets how close the camera starts (`start`; `tall` on a phone held upright) and how far the player may take it (`zoom`): [... omitted end of long line]\n160:- **The window and framing:** `cam.window = [48, 24]` is a dead zone (Super Mario World's): the camera stays still while the focus moves inside it and follows from its edge, so small steps don't jiggl [... omitted end of long line]\n167:- One shared screen: `cam.frame(heroes, { margin: 90 })` keeps everyone in view. A split screen: `game.splitScreen(2, { follow: [hero, hero2] })`, `layout: 'auto'` (side by side on a wide screen, stac [... omitted end of long line]\n171:- **Tweens** (Phaser's tweens, Unity's DOTween): `game.tween(target, { x: 10, y: 4 }, seconds, { ease, delay, repeat, yoyo, onDone, keep })` eases a target's numbers to new values, from where they are [... omitted end of long line]\n173:- **Paths:** `new E.Path(points, { closed, smooth: 'catmull' })` measures a line by distance along it: `at(d)` is a point with its heading (a moving platform's place, an enemy's dive, a rail, a camera [... omitted end of long line]\n174:- **Weather:** `game.weather = { kind, amount, wind, lightning }` (rain, snow, ash, leaves, sand): drops fall through the world's height in ground views and in three layers of parallax in side and ove [... omitted end of long line]\n180:- Wall `types[id] = { h, top, side, line, course, cut, cutH }`. `cut` lowers a wall when it stands between the camera and the floor.\n256:`E.Mover` is the ground views' answer to `Platformer`: a `Body` with a third-person game's movement.\n320:- Light every scene (the Look target's step 9): a dark game with no lights reads flat, and a judge says so. Canvas lighting leads because it draws the same in every browser and every headless check: s [... omitted end of long line]\n364:- **The modules:** `grid` (square and hex grids: A* paths, move ranges with climb and drop past allies, lines, symmetric fields of view, `E.Fog`, flood fills and groups, tactics' shapes of effect, fac [... omitted end of long line]\n371:- **The presentation sections** (Penner's easings beyond the core's, sprite frames and turns, tweens and scripts, paths, transitions, weather, input sequences, the camera's window and framing) are eac [... omitted end of long line]\n445:- Ships are sprites or vector parts drawn by code; a timeline array spawns waves by time or by how far the camera has come; enemies move on formulas (sine lines, dives aimed with `E.pattern.aim`) or a [... omitted end of long line]\n446:- Flyers keep up with the camera: each step add the scroll to their position (and to the bullets'), while the ground and the rock stay put.\n458:- Each step `race.update(dt, map)` (it moves every car), then the camera behind yours, turning after it more slowly than the kart turns (a drift shows): `m7.cam = cam; m7.chase({ x, y, angle: camAngle [... omitted end of long line]\n459:- Two players: `game.allowJoin({ max: 2 })`, `game.splitScreen(2, { layout: 'rows' })`, and in `draw` each viewport its own camera: `m7.draw(r, cams[r.viewport.i])`, `race.hud(r, players[r.viewport.i] [... omitted end of long line]\n41: *    interface (title, pause, settings, help, results, map screens and a HUD with a minimap) from data: new E.Shell(game,\n2400:    /** the E.Shell over this game (an HTML interface: screens and HUD), or null */\n2401:    this.shell = null;\n2547:    const sh = this.shell, s = this.scene, play = !!s && (!!s.pausable || this.sceneName === 'main');\n2563:    const fsChange = () => { this.input._refit(); if (this.shell && this.shell.screen) this.shell._render(); };   // (the player's choice is what they asked for: fullscreen.toggle() keeps it)\n2592:  _canBack() { const s = this.scene; return !!(this.shell && this.shell.screen) || !!s && (!!s.pausable || this.sceneName === 'main' || !!s.back); }\n2599:    const sh = this.shell, s = this.scene; if (sh && sh.screen) { sh.back(); return true; }\n2619:    const sh = this.shell, s = this.scene, I = this.input, fs = this.fullscreen, open = !!(sh && sh.screen);\n2829:    if (this.shell) this.shell.dispose();\n2938:    if (this.input.padLost) { this._autoPause('controller'); if (this.shell) this.shell.toast('Controller disconnected', 'Press a button on a controller to use it, or play on.'); else this.note('CONTR [... omitted end of long line]\n2939:    if (this.shell) this.shell._step();   // its screens move the focus with this step's input, and hold it back from the game\n2947:    const I = this.input, zr = !this.paused && !(this.shell && this.shell.screen) && !!this.zoomRange();\n2981:    if (F.keys !== false && !(this.shell && this.shell.screen) && !I.stickOn) { const m = I.move(), sp = (F.speed || 300) * dt; dx += m[0] * sp; dy += m[1] * sp; }   // (a finger pans by its drag, not [... omitted end of long line]\n3003:    if (this.paused && this.pauseOverlay && !(this.shell && this.shell._sys && this.shell.screen)) this.r.overlay(g => {\n3038: *    E.Shell draws the menu's screens (pause, settings, controls): section 21d.\n3098:    /** onChange(key, value): called after every change (E.Shell's settings.onChange goes through it) */\n3947:  /** open the standard save screen over the game (E.Shell's): 'save' (to a slot) or 'load'; done(save) after a load or\n3950:    const sh = this.game.shell; if (!sh || !sh._menu()) return false;\n4028:  this._needEl.style.display = this.shell && this.shell.screen ? 'none' : 'flex';   // (Settings open over it: hidden while it is)\n9343: *      const ui = new E.Shell(game, { theme: { accent: '#d9b77c' }, settings: { items: ['sound', 'volume', 'motion'] },\n9355: *    THE STANDARD MENU: every game gets one (new E.Game makes this shell for itself, and a game's own E.Shell takes over\n9361: *    false }, quit: 'title' } }) adjusts it; menu: false, or new E.Shell(game, { standard: false }), leaves it out.\n9365:.esh *{box-sizing:border-box}.esh [hidden]{display:none!important}.esh p{margin:4px 0 0;white-space:pre-line}\n9366:.esh h1,.esh h2{font-family:var(--title);font-weight:600;margin:2px 0 0;line-height:1.05}.esh h2{font-size:26px}\n9367:.esh-pan{background:var(--paper);border:1px solid var(--line);border-radius:6px;padding:10px 13px;box-shadow:0 8px 28px #0009}\n9368:.esh-k{font-size:11px;letter-spacing:.16em;text-transform:uppercase;color:var(--accent)}.esh-m{color:var(--muted);font-size:12px}\n9369:.esh-obj{position:absolute;left:var(--pl);top:var(--pt);max-width:min(330px,58vw)}.esh-obj b{font:600 17px var(--title);display:block}\n9370:.esh-dist{color:var(--accent);font-size:12px;margin-top:4px;letter-spacing:.06em}\n9371:.esh-vit{text-align:right;min-width:120px}.esh-hb{display:flex;gap:6px;pointer-events:auto}.esh-hb button{padding:6px 10px;font-size:11px;background:var(--paper)}\n9372:.esh-st{font-size:11px;letter-spacing:.16em}.esh-st i{display:inline-block;width:7px;height:7px;border-radius:50%;margin-right:6px;background:var(--c)}\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
