 owns network-specific browser suite.\n2. Fix integration defects; keep docs/verification.md count truthful. Three sim/save defects fixed+verified; title overflow minor fixed pending screenshot. New code changes require affected suites rerun, not unchanged coverage repeatedly.\n3. Build exit-interview.json exact TASK schema in root, all four feedback categories populated; build script embeds into About.\n4. Complete docs/verification.md and PROGRESS.md, npm run build then npm test on final HTML; ensure scripts reports actual counts and no runtime fetches.\n5. Deliver exact root HTML and interview with all required Source Information, Testing Feedback, Engine Feedback and Prompt Feedback in final chat. Usage exact '\"'added on import'; unknown for physical/WAN/listening facts.\n\n## Important implementation details\n\n- \"'`window.__NM` / NM.app exposes sim, net, game, ui, start, travel. Development test inspector mutation is separate from honest director.\n- App main uses engine120Hz; net.update in input hook continues through menus, live=true only online.\n- File:// needs no server. Hub browser script owns ephemeral127.0.0.1 server and shuts it by its own process.\n- Preserve parent repo changes and adjacent agent folders; no broad process cleanup.\n- Latest changes after original suite: authored enemy radius now applied; fog also marks adjacent boundary walls to make cave walls readable. Rerun affected sim/playthrough.\n- Existing scripts/build.mjs inlines all modules and full engine into root artifact and development index.html. No npm dependencies needed.\nEOF'","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
