{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_94","type":"agent_message","text":"The final checks found a co-op lifecycle issue: restoring an old checkpoint could bring back a departed ranger. That is fixed and covered by regression tests. Late join now preserves the expedition; I’m checking reconnection and refreshing the guardian screenshots before the last package test.\n"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_95","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"node --input-type=module <<'JS'\nimport fs from 'node:fs';const p='../exit-interview.json',d=JSON.parse(fs.readFileSync(p));d.sourceInformation.testing='Automated headless testing was permitted without a rendering performance budget. Checked the standard-rule full expedition, Chromium/WebKit, emulated DualSense and multitouch, measured Web Audio, real two-copy WebRTC and six unchanged Hub harness cases. Exact counts and reports are in docs/verification.md. Real controller/iPhone/TV, human listening and WAN/NAT reachability: unknown. First-player 18–25-minute pacing is unmeasured.';fs.writeFileSync(p,JSON.stringify(d,null,2)+'\\\\n');\nJS\nruff check --fix tests --select F,E9\nruff format tests\nnode scripts/build.mjs\nnpm test -- browser\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_95","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"node --input-type=module <<'JS'\nimport fs from 'node:fs';const p='../exit-interview.json',d=JSON.parse(fs.readFileSync(p));d.sourceInformation.testing='Automated headless testing was permitted without a rendering performance budget. Checked the standard-rule full expedition, Chromium/WebKit, emulated DualSense and multitouch, measured Web Audio, real two-copy WebRTC and six unchanged Hub harness cases. Exact counts and reports are in docs/verification.md. Real controller/iPhone/TV, human listening and WAN/NAT reachability: unknown. First-player 18–25-minute pacing is unmeasured.';fs.writeFileSync(p,JSON.stringify(d,null,2)+'\\\\n');\nJS\nruff check --fix tests --select F,E9\nruff format tests\nnode scripts/build.mjs\nnpm test -- browser\"","aggregated_output":"F841 Local variable `defects` is assigned to but never used\n  --> tests/browser.py:14:5\n   |\n12 | def run():\n13 |     count = 0\n14 |     defects = []\n   |     ^^^^^^^\n15 |     def check(value, message):\n16 |         nonlocal count\n   |\nhelp: Remove assignment to unused variable `defects`\n\nFound 1 error.\nNo fixes available (1 hidden fix can be enabled with the `--unsafe-fixes` option).\n2 files reformatted, 3 files left unchanged\nBuilt Advanced-Dungeons-Near-Misses-Advanced-Dungeons-and-Dragons-gpt-6.1-sol-max-20261106-035445.html (1,521,493 bytes)\nnpm notice run advanced-dungeons-near-misses@1.0.0 test\nnpm notice run node scripts/test.mjs browser\n97 checks passed; 0 suites failed.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_96","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"python3 - <<'PY'\np='tests/browser.py';s=open(p).read().replace('    defects = []\\\\n','');open(p,'w').write(s)\nPY\nruff check tests/browser.py --select F,E9\nruff format tests/browser.py\nnode --input-type=module <<'JS'\nimport fs from 'node:fs';const p='../exit-interview.json',d=JSON.parse(fs.readFileSync(p));d.testingFeedback[0]='Eight distinct defects were found and fixed: stale revival input, invalid saved actor coordinates, denied storage access at construction, title action overflow, touch HUD interception, ignored miniature palette options, checkpoint roster restoration and an asynchronous snapshot crossing a reconnection. Test-driver mistakes and repeated assertions are not counted.';d.testingFeedback[1]='Three defects were potentially game breaking: denied storage could stop startup, an invalid actor save could break resume, and an old checkpoint could restore a departed companion who then blocked progression. A separate high-severity reconnection snapshot race affected guest views. All have regression coverage.';fs.writeFileSync(p,JSON.stringify(d,null,2)+'\\\\n');\nJS\ncat > docs/verification.md <<'EOF'\n# Requirement / evidence ledger\n\nFinal verification is running against the packed root HTML. \"'`npm test` is the single quiet entry point; optional suite names restrict reruns after relevant changes. Verbose output is captured under docs/test-output.log. Counts below are actual assertions.\n\n| Requirement | Implementation | Evidence |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n|29 chambers / full tool graph / reserve budgets | content/campaign.js + shared Geometry.compile |152 content assertions; real optional lunch chamber documented in authoring.md |\n| Complete standard-rule expedition | production commands / fixed steps |17 full-clear assertions; playthrough-result.json:294.76 simulated seconds,58 arrows,52 banks,6 recoveries,1 ordinary death,0 voluntary restarts,all tools/both halves,assisted=false |\n| Swept arrows / recovery / survival / fog / acoustics / saves | sim + geometry + save |73 adversarial assertions, including current-roster restoration after joins/leaves |\n| Original native rigs and animation / draw immutability | render/art.js |95 native headless assertions; browser contact sheet and final scenes |\n| Original code-only audio /10% gain / focus / voices | audio/audio.js |73 headless +45 OfflineAudioContext/browser assertions (the45 are included in browser count) |\n| Validated protocol / action IDs / nonce epochs | net/network.js |38 protocol assertions including stale asynchronous pack/decode rejection |\n| Real standalone direct WebRTC | production data channel |10 transport assertions and11 actual full-game input/progression/latejoin assertions from file:// |\n| Hub lifecycle / true server / adverse network / departures | unchanged pinned harness |97 assertions across all six required final-artifact cases; hub-test-report.json |\n| Final-file controls, touch, menus, saves, attract, About, audio, WebKit | tests/browser.py |97 browser assertions; source/adverse/physical scopes recorded in browser-report.json |\n| Single-file package / pinned unchanged vendors / exact interview | build + package validator |31 assertions; same script order and metadata on delivered artifact |\n\nExpected full-suite total:694 checks. Replace this line with the actual final command result before delivery.\n\n## Confirmed defects\n\n- SIM-001 (major): stale held interaction could finish a revival beyond the heartbeat timeout. Added freshness validation; regression passed.\n- SAVE-001 (critical): a valid-checksummed envelope could contain invalid actor coordinates and break resume. Validated actors and restart state; regression passed.\n- SAVE-002 (critical): a denied localStorage property getter could stop construction. Guarded lookup with complete in-memory fallback; regression passed.\n- UI-001 (minor): initial TV title actions extended below the viewport. Bounded the card and compacted the action rows; viewport assertions passed.\n- UI-002 (major): touch tutorial content intercepted a natural movement thumb position. Moved/compacted touch HUD and made its text pass pointer input through; multitouch/cancel checks passed.\n- RENDER-001 (minor): miniature texture helper options used color instead of base/dark/light, silently retaining default palettes. Corrected actual helper arguments and reviewed rendered output.\n- SIM-002 (critical): restoring a checkpoint could resurrect a departed seat or remove a late seat. Reconciled restored actors to the current roster and validated both safe anchors; four regression assertions passed.\n- NET-001 (high): old asynchronous snapshot packing/decoding could finish in a fresh reconnection. Captured connection nonce and rejected stale completion; two regressions reproduce the old behavior and pass with the fix. Authority progression was unaffected.\n\nCount:8 distinct defects,3 potentially game breaking. Do not count test-director mistakes or repeated assertions. The network combat director was corrected to stop, aim and respect bow recovery against narrow moving rats; that was not a game defect. Initial stopped-clock visual captures were replaced with explicit `advance(...,{draw:true})` frames.\n\n## Presentation and external limits\n\nPurposeful screenshots: title-tv.png, cave-tv.png, guardian-amber.png, guardian-blue.png, results-tv.png and touch-portrait.png. Guardian/result screenshots use clearly separated developer fixtures and are not clear evidence; the command-only director proves completion.\n\nPhysical controller, real touch hardware, iPhone/iPad, living-room TV, human listening and WAN/NAT combinations are unknown. Standard pads and touch are emulated; WebKit is a secondary renderer, not real iOS certification. Audio evidence is measured signal, not human listening. The4m55s clear is an expert known-route replay, not a measured first-player18–25-minute session. First-player pacing remains unmeasured.\nEOF\nbiome check --write src scripts tests --max-diagnostics=5 > docs/biome-output.log 2>&1\nnode scripts/build.mjs'","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_96","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"python3 - <<'PY'\np='tests/browser.py';s=open(p).read().replace('    defects = []\\\\n','');open(p,'w').write(s)\nPY\nruff check tests/browser.py --select F,E9\nruff format tests/browser.py\nnode --input-type=module <<'JS'\nimport fs from 'node:fs';const p='../exit-interview.json',d=JSON.parse(fs.readFileSync(p));d.testingFeedback[0]='Eight distinct defects were found and fixed: stale revival input, invalid saved actor coordinates, denied storage access at construction, title action overflow, touch HUD interception, ignored miniature palette options, checkpoint roster restoration and an asynchronous snapshot crossing a reconnection. Test-driver mistakes and repeated assertions are not counted.';d.testingFeedback[1]='Three defects were potentially game breaking: denied storage could stop startup, an invalid actor save could break resume, and an old checkpoint could restore a departed companion who then blocked progression. A separate high-severity reconnection snapshot race affected guest views. All have regression coverage.';fs.writeFileSync(p,JSON.stringify(d,null,2)+'\\\\n');\nJS\ncat > docs/verification.md <<'EOF'\n# Requirement / evidence ledger\n\nFinal verification is running against the packed root HTML. \"'`npm test` is the single quiet entry point; optional suite names restrict reruns after relevant changes. Verbose output is captured under docs/test-output.log. Counts below are actual assertions.\n\n| Requirement | Implementation | Evidence |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n|29 chambers / full tool graph / reserve budgets | content/campaign.js + shared Geometry.compile |152 content assertions; real optional lunch chamber documented in authoring.md |\n| Complete standard-rule expedition | production commands / fixed steps |17 full-clear assertions; playthrough-result.json:294.76 simulated seconds,58 arrows,52 banks,6 recoveries,1 ordinary death,0 voluntary restarts,all tools/both halves,assisted=false |\n| Swept arrows / recovery / survival / fog / acoustics / saves | sim + geometry + save |73 adversarial assertions, including current-roster restoration after joins/leaves |\n| Original native rigs and animation / draw immutability | render/art.js |95 native headless assertions; browser contact sheet and final scenes |\n| Original code-only audio /10% gain / focus / voices | audio/audio.js |73 headless +45 OfflineAudioContext/browser assertions (the45 are included in browser count) |\n| Validated protocol / action IDs / nonce epochs | net/network.js |38 protocol assertions including stale asynchronous pack/decode rejection |\n| Real standalone direct WebRTC | production data channel |10 transport assertions and11 actual full-game input/progression/latejoin assertions from file:// |\n| Hub lifecycle / true server / adverse network / departures | unchanged pinned harness |97 assertions across all six required final-artifact cases; hub-test-report.json |\n| Final-file controls, touch, menus, saves, attract, About, audio, WebKit | tests/browser.py |97 browser assertions; source/adverse/physical scopes recorded in browser-report.json |\n| Single-file package / pinned unchanged vendors / exact interview | build + package validator |31 assertions; same script order and metadata on delivered artifact |\n\nExpected full-suite total:694 checks. Replace this line with the actual final command result before delivery.\n\n## Confirmed defects\n\n- SIM-001 (major): stale held interaction could finish a revival beyond the heartbeat timeout. Added freshness validation; regression passed.\n- SAVE-001 (critical): a valid-checksummed envelope could contain invalid actor coordinates and break resume. Validated actors and restart state; regression passed.\n- SAVE-002 (critical): a denied localStorage property getter could stop construction. Guarded lookup with complete in-memory fallback; regression passed.\n- UI-001 (minor): initial TV title actions extended below the viewport. Bounded the card and compacted the action rows; viewport assertions passed.\n- UI-002 (major): touch tutorial content intercepted a natural movement thumb position. Moved/compacted touch HUD and made its text pass pointer input through; multitouch/cancel checks passed.\n- RENDER-001 (minor): miniature texture helper options used color instead of base/dark/light, silently retaining default palettes. Corrected actual helper arguments and reviewed rendered output.\n- SIM-002 (critical): restoring a checkpoint could resurrect a departed seat or remove a late seat. Reconciled restored actors to the current roster and validated both safe anchors; four regression assertions passed.\n- NET-001 (high): old asynchronous snapshot packing/decoding could finish in a fresh reconnection. Captured connection nonce and rejected stale completion; two regressions reproduce the old behavior and pass with the fix. Authority progression was unaffected.\n\nCount:8 distinct defects,3 potentially game breaking. Do not count test-director mistakes or repeated assertions. The network combat director was corrected to stop, aim and respect bow recovery against narrow moving rats; that was not a game defect. Initial stopped-clock visual captures were replaced with explicit `advance(...,{draw:true})` frames.\n\n## Presentation and external limits\n\nPurposeful screenshots: title-tv.png, cave-tv.png, guardian-amber.png, guardian-blue.png, results-tv.png and touch-portrait.png. Guardian/result screenshots use clearly separated developer fixtures and are not clear evidence; the command-only director proves completion.\n\nPhysical controller, real touch hardware, iPhone/iPad, living-room TV, human listening and WAN/NAT combinations are unknown. Standard pads and touch are emulated; WebKit is a secondary renderer, not real iOS certification. Audio evidence is measured signal, not human listening. The4m55s clear is an expert known-route replay, not a measured first-player18–25-minute session. First-player pacing remains unmeasured.\nEOF\nbiome check --write src scripts tests --max-diagnostics=5 > docs/biome-output.log 2>&1\nnode scripts/build.mjs'","aggregated_output":"All checks passed!\n1 file left unchanged\nBuilt Advanced-Dungeons-Near-Misses-Advanced-Dungeons-and-Dragons-gpt-6.1-sol-max-20261106-035445.html (1,521,886 bytes)\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
